1result.sql is the most reliable:

• It converts insert_date to DATE() everywhere, guaranteeing the “day” comparisons work even if a time‑of‑day ever appears.  
• It collapses the day list with GROUP BY d before building the streak, so the longest‑run logic can’t be distorted by multiple rows on the same day.  
• The rest of the calculation (rows in longest span, capital share) is then applied to the full, un‑deduplicated rows – giving the right counts (5 rows, 1 capital row, 0.2000).  
• 0result.sql skips DATE() in parts of the streak logic, while 2result.sql is just a more verbose variant of 1result.sql with no extra benefit.

So the correct script is:

```plaintext
1result.sql
```